    </Tags>
    <Programs>
      <Program Name="FandG_Angola" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="MainRoutine" Disabled="false">
        <Tags/>
        <Routines>
          <Routine Name="MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: _MAIN rung 3 (GE) - %S00001 (#FST_SCN) NOCON; CALL Init]
First-scan call: NO #FST_SCN (%S00001, i.e. S:FS) guards CALL Init, so the Init block runs on the first scan only and resets the two internal cause-and-effect alarm flags and clears the start-up delay/timer registers there. The printed legend above the rung reads 'Call initiate'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(S:FS)JSR(Init,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: _MAIN rung 5 (GE) - %S00001 (#FST_SCN) NCCON; CALL Input]
NC #FST_SCN (%S00001, i.e. XIO(S:FS) = NOT first scan) guards CALL Input, so the input-handling block runs on every scan except the first. The printed legend reads 'Call Input routine'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(S:FS)JSR(Input,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: _MAIN rung 7 (GE) - %S00001 (#FST_SCN) NCCON; CALL Logic]
NC #FST_SCN (%S00001, i.e. XIO(S:FS)) guards CALL Logic on every scan after the first. The legend calls it 'Call LogicCE (Cause & Effect) routine' but the CALL operand - and therefore the JSR target - is the GE routine Logic.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(S:FS)JSR(Logic,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Poll Modbus communication from Murphy engine panels via MVI56E-MCM module]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(S:FS)JSR(Modbus_Comm,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: _MAIN rung 9 (GE) - %S00001 (#FST_SCN) NCCON; CALL Output]
NC #FST_SCN (%S00001, i.e. XIO(S:FS)) guards CALL Output on every scan after the first, so the physical outputs are driven only once the first scan is over. The printed legend reads 'Call Output routine'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(S:FS)JSR(Output,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Init" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Initialize pump and system delay timers at first scan]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[MOV(0,Pump_Timer1[0]),MOV(0,System_C_E_Delay[0])];]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Unlatch acoustic alarm commands at initial power up]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[OTU(Tag_DO_15_INT),OTU(SA_7404_001_002_INT)];]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Clear pump timer accumulator]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[MOV(0,Pump_Timer1[0]);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Input" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Map physical input modules (Slot 7 DI, Slots 2-4 AI, Slot 6 HART) into program tags]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(IO_Mapping_In,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Input rung 3 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL DI_1]
Unconditional call of the DI_1 block, which reads the first 16 digital inputs %I0001-%I0016 of the PLC input module and derives their alarm / alarm-inhibit bits (printed legend: 'Inputs %I0001 to %I0016 PLC Input module.'). #ALW_ON (%S00007) is always true, so the JSR is unconditional.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(DI_1,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Input rung 5 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL DI_2]
Unconditional call of the DI_2 block, the second digital-input handler (printed legend: 'Inputs %I0017 to %I0032 PLC Input module.'). The DI_2 body in this export is comment-only, so the call currently transfers control to an empty routine; it is kept because the printed call structure contains it.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(DI_2,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Input rung 7 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL AI_1]
Unconditional call of the AI_1 block, the first analogue-input handler (printed legend: 'Inputs %AI0001 to %AI008 PLC Input module.'). #ALW_ON (%S00007) is always true, so the JSR is unconditional.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(AI_1,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Input rung 9 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL AI_2]
Unconditional call of the AI_2 block, the second analogue-input handler (printed legend: 'Inputs %AI0009 to %AI016 PLC Input module.').]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(AI_2,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Input rung 11 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL AI_3]
Unconditional call of the AI_3 block, the third analogue-input handler (printed legend: 'Inputs %AI0017 to %AI024 PLC Input module.').]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(AI_3,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Input rung 13 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL Vote_1]
Unconditional call of the Vote_1 block, which does the voting of the input signals (printed legend: 'Voting of input signals.'). It is the last rung of the block and runs every scan.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(Vote_1,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="DI_1" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 4 (GE) - %I00001, %M00001; NOCON -> COIL]
6401-ZSH-001 ESD-valve-open digital input %I00001 drives its alarm bit ZSH_6401_001_AL (%M00001) straight through. The source note for %I0001 reads 'Generates no latched alarms', and the rung is printed as a single NO contact into a plain coil with no reset contact.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(ZSH_6401_001)OTE(ZSH_6401_001_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 5 (GE) - %M00001, %M00033; NOCON -> COIL]
Alarm-inhibit (cause-and-effect) bit ZSH_6401_001_ALI (%M00033) repeats ZSH_6401_001_AL (%M00001). This channel has no _INH symbol in the source symbol table, so the printed rung carries only the one NO contact.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(ZSH_6401_001_AL)OTE(ZSH_6401_001_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 7 (GE) - %I00002, %M00002; NOCON -> COIL]
6401-ZSL-001 ESD-valve-closed digital input %I00002 drives ZSL_6401_001_AL (%M00002) with a plain coil. The source note for %I0002 reads 'Generates no latched alarms', so there is no seal-in or reset contact.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(ZSL_6401_001)OTE(ZSL_6401_001_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 8 (GE) - %M00002, %M00034; NOCON -> COIL]
Alarm-inhibit bit ZSL_6401_001_ALI (%M00034) repeats ZSL_6401_001_AL (%M00002). No _INH symbol exists for this channel, so only the single NO contact is printed.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(ZSL_6401_001_AL)OTE(ZSL_6401_001_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 10 (GE) - %I00003, %M00700, %M00003; NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
7503-FS-001 stop-foam push-button %I00003 drives FS_7503_001_AL (%M00003) through a NC System_Reset (%M00700) contact, so the bit is forced off while the system reset is held. The source note says %I0003 generates no latched alarms, so no seal-in branch is drawn - the reset contact is in series only.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(FS_7503_001)XIO(System_Reset)OTE(FS_7503_001_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 11 (GE) - %M00003, %M00099, %M00035; NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
FS_7503_001_ALI (%M00035) = FS_7503_001_AL (%M00003) AND NOT FS_7503_001_INH (%M00099), the cause-and-effect alarm bit consumed by Sound/CE_LOG/Vote_1.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(FS_7503_001_AL)XIO(FS_7503_001_INH)OTE(FS_7503_001_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 13 (GE) + parallel branch row (page 1, row 504.0; BUS x=172) - %I00004, %M00004, %M00700; NOCON, NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
Latched alarm for 7503-LS-001 AFFF tank low level: NO input %I00004 picks up LS_7503_001_AL (%M00004) and the parallel NO contact of LS_7503_001_AL (branch row joined by the bus at x=172) seals it in. The NC System_Reset (%M00700) contact sits to the right of the branch, so reset dominates and clears the latch - the drawn equivalent of set/reset in one rung.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(LS_7503_001),XIC(LS_7503_001_AL)]XIO(System_Reset)OTE(LS_7503_001_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 14 (GE) - %M00004, %M00100, %M00036; NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
LS_7503_001_ALI (%M00036) = LS_7503_001_AL (%M00004) AND NOT LS_7503_001_INH (%M00100).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(LS_7503_001_AL)XIO(LS_7503_001_INH)OTE(LS_7503_001_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 16 (GE) + parallel branch row (page 2, row 127.3; BUS x=172) - %I00005, %M00005, %M00700; NOCON, NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
Latched alarm for 7503-LS-002 Diesel tank low level: NO input %I00005 picks up LS_7503_002_AL (%M00005), sealed in by its own NO contact in the parallel branch, with NC System_Reset (%M00700) in series to the right of the branch - the same seal-in-with-reset pattern as rung 13.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(LS_7503_002),XIC(LS_7503_002_AL)]XIO(System_Reset)OTE(LS_7503_002_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 17 (GE) - %M00005, %M00101, %M00037; NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
LS_7503_002_ALI (%M00037) = LS_7503_002_AL (%M00005) AND NOT LS_7503_002_INH (%M00101).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(LS_7503_002_AL)XIO(LS_7503_002_INH)OTE(LS_7503_002_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 19 (GE) - %I00006, %M00006; NOCON -> COIL]
Pulsed input %I00006 from output Q05 (pump A out signal) drives Pump_A_PulsIn_AL (%M00006) with a plain coil. The source note for %I0006 reads 'Generates nolatched alarms', so no latch or reset contact is drawn.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn)OTE(Pump_A_PulsIn_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 20 (GE) - %M00006, %M00038; NOCON -> COIL]
Pump_A_PulsIn_ALI (%M00038) repeats Pump_A_PulsIn_AL (%M00006). No _INH symbol exists for this pulsed channel, so only the one NO contact is printed.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn_AL)OTE(Pump_A_PulsIn_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 22 (GE) - %I00007, %M00007; NOCON -> COIL]
Pulsed input %I00007 from output Q07 (pump B start signal) drives Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_AL (%M00007) with a plain coil. The source note for %I0007 reads 'Generates nolatched alarms'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn)OTE(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="13" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 23 (GE) - %M00007, %M00039; NOCON -> COIL]
Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_ALI (%M00039) repeats Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_AL (%M00007); no inhibit symbol exists for this channel.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_AL)OTE(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="14" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 25 (GE) - %I00008, %M00008; NOCON -> COIL]
Spare digital input SpareDI_08 (%I00008) drives SpareDI_08_AL (%M00008) with a plain coil. The source note for %I0008 reads 'Generates nolatched alarms'; the spare follows the same two-rung pattern as the used channels.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SpareDI_08)OTE(SpareDI_08_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="15" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 26 (GE) - %M00008, %M00040; NOCON -> COIL]
SpareDI_08_ALI (%M00040) repeats SpareDI_08_AL (%M00008); no _INH symbol exists for the spare.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SpareDI_08_AL)OTE(SpareDI_08_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="16" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 28 (GE) - %I00009, %M00009; NOCON -> COIL]
Standby-pump-B-inhibited input %I00009 drives Pump_B_Inhibited_AL (%M00009) with a plain coil. The source note for %I0009 reads 'Generates nolatched alarms'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_B_Inhibited)OTE(Pump_B_Inhibited_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="17" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 29 (GE) - %M00009, %M00041; NOCON -> COIL]
Pump_B_Inhibited_ALI (%M00041) repeats Pump_B_Inhibited_AL (%M00009); no inhibit symbol exists for this channel.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_B_Inhibited_AL)OTE(Pump_B_Inhibited_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="18" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 31 (GE) - %I00010, %M00010; NCCON -> COIL]
6401-ESDV-001 ESD fuel-gas push-button %I00010 is a fail-safe NC field contact, so the drawn NC contact alarms ESDV_6401_001_AL (%M00010) when the input opens. Plain coil - the source note for %I0010 reads 'Generates nolatched alarms'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(ESDV_6401_001)OTE(ESDV_6401_001_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="19" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 32 (GE) - %M00010, %M00042; NOCON -> COIL]
ESDV_6401_001_ALI (%M00042) repeats ESDV_6401_001_AL (%M00010); no inhibit symbol exists for the ESDV channel.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(ESDV_6401_001_AL)OTE(ESDV_6401_001_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="20" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 34 (GE) + parallel branch row (page 4, row 536.4; BUS x=172) - %I00011, %M00011, %M00700; NOCON, NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
Latched alarm for spare input SpareDI_11: NO input %I00011 picks up SpareDI_11_AL (%M00011), the parallel NO contact of SpareDI_11_AL seals it in, and the NC System_Reset (%M00700) contact to the right of the branch clears it - identical seal-in pattern to rungs 13 and 16, so the spare channel latches too.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(SpareDI_11),XIC(SpareDI_11_AL)]XIO(System_Reset)OTE(SpareDI_11_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="21" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 35 (GE) - %M00011, %M00107, %M00043; NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
SpareDI_11_ALI (%M00043) = SpareDI_11_AL (%M00011) AND NOT SpareDI_11_INH (%M00107).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SpareDI_11_AL)XIO(SpareDI_11_INH)OTE(SpareDI_11_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="22" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 37 (GE) - %I00012, %M00700, %M00012; NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
Foam-release-inhibit input %I00012 drives INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_AL (%M00012) with a NC System_Reset (%M00700) contact in series; the bit is forced off while reset is held.
!! REVIEW: AMBIGUOUS: the printed channel note for %I0012 claims 'Generates latched alarms', but the drawn rung has no seal-in branch (no BUS anywhere on pages 4-5 other than rung 34) and there is no SETCOIL/RESETCOIL, so as printed the bit is level-with-reset-override, not latched. Transcribed exactly as drawn - confirm whether the seal-in branch was omitted in the source export.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL)XIO(System_Reset)OTE(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="23" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 38 (GE) - %M00012, %M00108, %M00044; NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI (%M00044) = INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_AL (%M00012) AND NOT INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_INH (%M00108); per the source cross reference this bit is read by Vote_1 rung 6 and by Loc_Al.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_AL)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_INH)OTE(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="24" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 40 (GE) - %I00013, %M00700, %M00013; NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
All-outputs-inhibit input %I00013 drives INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_AL (%M00013) with a NC System_Reset (%M00700) contact in series, so the bit is forced off while the system reset is held.
!! REVIEW: AMBIGUOUS: the printed channel note for %I0013 claims 'Generates latched alarms', but no seal-in branch and no SETCOIL/RESETCOIL are drawn (page 5 has no BUS at all), so as printed the bit is level-with-reset-override. Transcribed exactly as drawn - confirm source intent.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS)XIO(System_Reset)OTE(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_AL);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="25" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: DI_1 rung 41 (GE) - %M00013, %M00109, %M00045; NOCON, NCCON -> COIL]
INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI (%M00045) = INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_AL (%M00013) AND NOT INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_INH (%M00109); the source cross reference shows it read by Shutdown, Protect, Sound, Logic and CE_LOG.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_AL)XIO(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_INH)OTE(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="DI_2" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Source routine is empty (comment-only in the GE program). Placeholder rung so the routine can be retained.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[NOP();]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
