          <Routine Name="Vote_1" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Vote_1 rung 2 (GE, page 0) - DG_7404_001..010_ALLI NO contacts (%M00425-%M00434); the ten branches are wrapped on the sheet as 4 contact rows x 3 contact columns (columns x=25-100, 172-243, 315-387) of one OR chain; OTE Voting_DG_7404_ALLI %M00605]
Voting of the low alarm (_ALLI) of the pump-house IR point gas detectors: any of the ten DG_7404_001..010 low alarms (%M00425-%M00434, all NO contacts) operates Voting_DG_7404_ALLI (%M00605), which the cause & effect routine CE_LOG uses. The sheet wraps the ten parallel branches of this one OR chain into three contact columns joined by the bracket wires.
!! REVIEW: VERIFICATION ITEM: the printed mesh is read as a plain OR of all contacts (the columns are a sheet-layout wrap of one OR chain). The alternative reading is one alarm per detector column AND-ed across columns; it is rejected because the same drawing convention would make Voting_All_Inhibits require an inhibit in every column. Confirm against the Proficy source before deployment.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(DG_7404_001_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_002_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_003_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_004_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_005_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_006_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_007_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_008_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_009_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_010_ALLI)]OTE(Voting_DG_7404_ALLI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Vote_1 rung 4 (GE, page 1) - DG_7404_001..010_ALHI NO contacts (%M00377-%M00386); the ten branches are wrapped on the sheet as 4 contact rows x 3 contact columns (columns x=25-100, 172-243, 315-387) of one OR chain; OTE Voting_DG_7404_ALHI %M00606]
Voting of the high alarm (_ALHI) of the pump-house IR point gas detectors: any of the ten DG_7404_001..010 high alarms (%M00377-%M00386, all NO contacts) operates Voting_DG_7404_ALHI (%M00606) for the cause & effect routine CE_LOG. Same drawing convention as rung 2 - three wrapped columns of one OR chain.
!! REVIEW: VERIFICATION ITEM: the printed mesh is read as a plain OR of all contacts (the columns are a sheet-layout wrap of one OR chain). The alternative reading is one alarm per detector column AND-ed across columns; it is rejected because the same drawing convention would make Voting_All_Inhibits require an inhibit in every column. Confirm against the Proficy source before deployment.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(DG_7404_001_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_002_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_003_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_004_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_005_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_006_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_007_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_008_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_009_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_010_ALHI)]OTE(Voting_DG_7404_ALHI);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Vote_1 rungs 6+7 (GE, pages 2-3) - printed rung 6 ends in a horizontal connector ('+' circle, no operand) that reappears as the '+' element at the start of printed rung 7, so both meshes are one net: 32 _INH contacts (%M00097-%M00128, 5 columns) OR-ed with 24 _INH contacts (%M00449-%M00472, 4 columns); OTE Voting_All_Inhibits %M00607]
Voting of all inhibits from all inputs. The digital-input inhibit bits (%M00097-%M00128, 32 NO contacts) are OR-ed with the analogue inhibit field %M00449-%M00472 (24 NO contacts) to drive Voting_All_Inhibits (%M00607). Printed rung 6 ends in a horizontal connector - the un-named '+' circle is the same node as the '+' contact opening printed rung 7 - so the two meshes are one net, emitted as one Logix rung; DG_7404_011R_INH (%M00462) legitimately appears twice in printed rung 7.
!! REVIEW: VERIFICATION ITEM: the printed mesh is read as a plain OR of all contacts (the columns are a sheet-layout wrap of one OR chain). The alternative reading is one alarm per detector column AND-ed across columns; it is rejected because the same drawing convention would make Voting_All_Inhibits require an inhibit in every column. Confirm against the Proficy source before deployment.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(ZSH_6401_001_INH),XIC(ZSL_6401_001_INH),XIC(FS_7503_001_INH),XIC(LS_7503_001_INH),XIC(LS_7503_002_INH),XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn_INH),XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_INH),XIC(SpareDI_08_INH),XIC(Pump_B_Inhibited_INH),XIC(ESDV_6401_001_INH),XIC(SpareDI_11_INH),XIC(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_INH),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_INH),XIC(SpareDI_14_INH),XIC(SpareDI_15_INH),XIC(SpareDI_16_INH),XIC(SpareDI_17_INH),XIC(SpareDI_18_INH),XIC(SpareDI_19_INH),XIC(SpareDI_20_INH),XIC(SpareDI_21_INH),XIC(SpareDI_22_INH),XIC(SpareDI_23_INH),XIC(SpareDI_24_INH),XIC(SpareDI_25_INH),XIC(SpareDI_26_INH),XIC(SpareDI_27_INH),XIC(SpareDI_28_INH),XIC(SpareDI_29_INH),XIC(SpareDI_30_INH),XIC(SpareDI_31_INH),XIC(SpareDI_32_INH),XIC(DG_7404_001_INH),XIC(DG_7404_002_INH),XIC(DG_7404_003_INH),XIC(DG_7404_004_INH),XIC(DG_7404_005_INH),XIC(DG_7404_006_INH),XIC(DG_7404_007_INH),XIC(DG_7404_008_INH),XIC(DG_7404_009_INH),XIC(DG_7404_010_INH),XIC(DG_7404_011R_INH),XIC(DF_7404_001_INH),XIC(DF_7404_002_INH),XIC(SpareAI_15_INH),XIC(SpareAI_16_INH),XIC(PST_7002_001_INH),XIC(PST_6401_001_INH),XIC(PST_7503_001_INH),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_INH),XIC(SpareAI_21_INH),XIC(FR_7503_003_INH),XIC(SpareAI_23_INH),XIC(SpareAI_24_INH)]OTE(Voting_All_Inhibits);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Vote_1 rungs 9+10 (GE, pages 5 and 7) - printed rung 9 ends in a horizontal connector ('+' circle, no operand) matched by the '+' element at the start of printed rung 10: 32 _OC contacts (%M00129-%M00160, 5 columns) OR-ed with 49 _OC/_SC contacts (%M00473-%M00520 plus DG_7404_011R_FLT1 %M00534, 5 columns); OTE Voting_All_Faults %M00608]
Voting of all faults from all inputs. The digital-input open-circuit bits (%M00129-%M00160, 32 NO contacts) are OR-ed with the analogue open/short-circuit fault field of printed rung 10 (%M00473-%M00520 and DG_7404_011R_FLT1 %M00534, 49 NO contacts) to drive Voting_All_Faults (%M00608). Printed rung 9 ends in the same horizontal connector ('+' circle) matched by the '+' contact opening printed rung 10, so both meshes are one net, emitted as one Logix rung.
!! REVIEW: VERIFICATION ITEM: the printed mesh is read as a plain OR of all contacts (the columns are a sheet-layout wrap of one OR chain). The alternative reading is one alarm per detector column AND-ed across columns; it is rejected because the same drawing convention would make Voting_All_Inhibits require an inhibit in every column. Confirm against the Proficy source before deployment.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(ZSH_6401_001_OC),XIC(ZSL_6401_001_OC),XIC(FS_7503_001_OC),XIC(LS_7503_001_OC),XIC(LS_7503_002_OC),XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn_OC),XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_OC),XIC(SpareDI_08_OC),XIC(Pump_B_Inhibited_OC),XIC(ESDV_6401_001_OC),XIC(SpareDI_11_OC),XIC(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_OC),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_OC),XIC(SpareDI_14_OC),XIC(SpareDI_15_OC),XIC(SpareDI_16_OC),XIC(SpareDI_17_OC),XIC(SpareDI_18_OC),XIC(SpareDI_19_OC),XIC(SpareDI_20_OC),XIC(SpareDI_21_OC),XIC(SpareDI_22_OC),XIC(SpareDI_23_OC),XIC(SpareDI_24_OC),XIC(SpareDI_25_OC),XIC(SpareDI_26_OC),XIC(SpareDI_27_OC),XIC(SpareDI_28_OC),XIC(SpareDI_29_OC),XIC(SpareDI_30_OC),XIC(SpareDI_31_OC),XIC(SpareDI_32_OC),XIC(DG_7404_001_OC),XIC(DG_7404_001_SC),XIC(DG_7404_002_OC),XIC(DG_7404_002_SC),XIC(DG_7404_003_OC),XIC(DG_7404_003_SC),XIC(DG_7404_004_OC),XIC(DG_7404_004_SC),XIC(DG_7404_005_OC),XIC(DG_7404_005_SC),XIC(DG_7404_006_OC),XIC(DG_7404_006_SC),XIC(DG_7404_007_OC),XIC(DG_7404_007_SC),XIC(DG_7404_008_OC),XIC(DG_7404_008_SC),XIC(DG_7404_009_OC),XIC(DG_7404_009_SC),XIC(DG_7404_010_OC),XIC(DG_7404_010_SC),XIC(SpareAI_11_OC),XIC(SpareAI_11_SC),XIC(DF_7404_001_OC),XIC(DF_7404_001_SC),XIC(DF_7404_002_OC),XIC(DF_7404_002_SC),XIC(DG_7404_011R_OC),XIC(DG_7404_011R_SC),XIC(SpareAI_15_OC),XIC(SpareAI_15_SC),XIC(SpareAI_16_OC),XIC(SpareAI_16_SC),XIC(PST_7002_001_OC),XIC(PST_7002_001_SC),XIC(PST_6401_001_OC),XIC(PST_6401_001_SC),XIC(PST_7503_001_OC),XIC(PST_7503_001_SC),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_OC),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_SC),XIC(SpareAI_21_OC),XIC(SpareAI_21_SC),XIC(FR_7503_003_OC),XIC(FR_7503_003_SC),XIC(SpareAI_23_OC),XIC(SpareAI_23_SC),XIC(SpareAI_24_OC),XIC(SpareAI_24_SC),XIC(DG_7404_011R_FLT1)]OTE(Voting_All_Faults);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[1.0 second clock generator: 1000 ms self-resetting timer for pulsing flashers/indicators.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(TMR_T_SEC.DN)TON(TMR_T_SEC,1000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[1.0 second square wave pulse: 500 ms ON / 500 ms OFF.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[LES(TMR_T_SEC.ACC,500)OTE(T_SEC_PULSE);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[1.0 minute clock generator: 60,000 ms self-resetting timer for wire-supervision pulse testing.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(TMR_T_MIN.DN)TON(TMR_T_MIN,60000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[1.0 minute square wave pulse: 30 s ON / 30 s OFF.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[LES(TMR_T_MIN.ACC,30000)OTE(T_MIN_PULSE);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Master System Reset: Triggered by panel PB E11 (TB-07 21&22), HMI touch button, auto startup reset, or first scan]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(System_Reset_PB),XIC(System_Reset_HMI),XIC(System_Reset_Startup),XIC(S:FS)]OTE(System_Reset);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Native Logix HMI Reset timer: holds System_Reset_HMI active for 5.0 seconds (5000 ms, matching GE ONDTR 50 tenths) before auto-clearing.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(System_Reset_HMI)TON(TMR_HMI_Reset,5000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[When the 2.0-second HMI reset timer completes, automatically unlatch System_Reset_HMI back to 0 and reset the timer.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_HMI_Reset.DN)[OTU(System_Reset_HMI),RES(TMR_HMI_Reset)];]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Read controller minor-fault bits every scan. Replaces GE system bits #LOW_BAT, #LOS_IOM, #HRD_FLT used by the Sound routine (PLC_Fault annunciation).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[GSV(FaultLog,,MinorFaultBits,Sys_MinorFaultBits);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Battery / energy-storage minor fault (bit 10) -> SYS_LOW_BAT (GE #LOW_BAT).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Sys_MinorFaultBits.10)OTE(SYS_LOW_BAT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[I/O minor fault, e.g. lost module connection (bit 3) -> SYS_LOS_IOM (GE #LOS_IOM). Requires I/O modules configured NOT to major-fault the controller on connection loss.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Sys_MinorFaultBits.3)OTE(SYS_LOS_IOM);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Program (bit 4) or watchdog (bit 6) minor fault -> SYS_HRD_FLT (GE #HRD_FLT).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(Sys_MinorFaultBits.4),XIC(Sys_MinorFaultBits.6)]OTE(SYS_HRD_FLT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Clear controller minor-fault bits on System Reset (replaces GE MOVE 0/1 + SVC_REQ 14 'clear PLC/IO fault table'). S:MINOR is a read-only status flag in Logix, so the documented SSV FaultLog.MinorFaultBits method is used.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(System_Reset)SSV(FaultLog,,MinorFaultBits,Sys_FaultClearZero);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Detector warm-up delay timer: 120 seconds (120,000 ms) before Cause & Effect trip logic is enabled.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[TON(TMR_C_E_Delay,120000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="13" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[T00002 turns ON when the 120-second detector warm-up timer completes.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_C_E_Delay.DN)OTE(T00002);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="14" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Auto-reset at 118 seconds (2.0 s before the 120s warm-up completes): pulses System_Reset_Startup to wipe warm-up spikes before C&E logic goes live.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[GEQ(TMR_C_E_Delay.ACC,118000)XIO(TMR_C_E_Delay.DN)OTE(System_Reset_Startup);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="15" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Execute Cause & Effect shutdown logic (CE_LOG) once detector warm-up delay is complete (T00002 = 1).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(T00002)JSR(CE_LOG,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="16" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Execute Sounder and Alarm horn routine on all scans except first scan.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(S:FS)JSR(Sound,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="CE_LOG" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Cause & Effect trips for P2100/P2200, P3600/P3700 booster pumps and PumpShutdown: activated on any high gas voting, open-path gas, fire detectors, ESD valve closed, or deluge pressure switch.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(Voting_DG_7404_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_011R_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_003_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_001_ALHI),XIC(PST_6401_001_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_002_ALHI),XIC(ZSL_6401_001_ALI),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI),XIC(ESDV_6401_001_ALI)][OTE(P2100_P2200_INT),OTE(P3600_P3700_INT),OTE(PumpShutdown_INT)];]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 5 (GE), page 1 row 32.76 - NO contacts %M00606 %M00390 %M00398 %M00388 %M00389 %M00394 %M00396 in parallel -> OTE %M00225]
Cause and effect, ESD fuel gas valve: the same fire/gas causes except the ESD valve button - gas voting %M00606, 7404-DG-011R %M00390, 7503-FR-003 %M00398, 7503-FR-001/002 %M00396, 7404-DF-001 %M00388, 7404-DF-002 %M00389 and 6401-PST-001 %M00394 - are seven parallel branches on one node that drives EY_6401_001_002_INT %M00225 (6401-EY-001/002 ESD fuel gas valve shutdown).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(Voting_DG_7404_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_011R_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_003_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_001_ALHI),XIC(PST_6401_001_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_002_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI)]OTE(EY_6401_001_002_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 8 (GE), page 2 row 32.76 - NO %M00388 %M00389 %M00396 %M00398 %M00229 in parallel, then NO %M00035, NC %M00700, NC %M00621 -> OTE %M00229]
Start of pump A: flame detector 7404-DF-001 %M00388, 7404-DF-002 %M00389, foam release 7503-FR-001/002 %M00396, 7503-FR-003 %M00398 or the pump's own seal-in contact PUMP_A_INT %M00229 request the deluge pump. The request is passed only while the stop foam button 7503-FS-001 %M00035 is not inhibited, System_Reset %M00700 is not pushed and the 60-minute run limit Pump_Active_1_Hour %M00621 is not reached; the result latches PUMP_A_INT %M00229.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(DF_7404_001_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_002_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_003_ALHI),XIC(PUMP_A_INT)]XIC(FS_7503_001_ALI)XIO(System_Reset)XIO(Pump_Active_1_Hour)OTE(PUMP_A_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 9 (GE), page 2 row 807.48 - NO %M00229, NO #T_SEC %S00005 -> UPCTR %R00245 (Pump_Timer13) PV 3600 -> OTE %M00621]
Pump A active-hour counter: GE UPCTR with register Pump_Timer13 %R00245 and preset PV 3600 counts the #T_SEC one-second pulse %S00005 while PUMP_A_INT %M00229 is on, i.e. it times out after 60 minutes. Converted to CTU tag CTR_Pump_A_Hour with preset 3600.
!! REVIEW: AMBIGUOUS: the R (reset) input of the UPCTR is wired to 7503-FS-001 %M00035, System_Reset %M00700 and the counter's own done bit Pump_Active_1_Hour %M00621 in parallel, so the counter clears itself as soon as it reaches 3600 and Pump_Active_1_Hour %M00621 is true for a single scan only. That self-reset is reproduced exactly as printed.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(PUMP_A_INT)XIC(T_SEC_PULSE)CTU(CTR_Pump_A_Hour,3600,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 9 (GE), page 2 row 807.48 - derived: counter done -> OTE %M00621]
Done contact of the pump A active-hour counter drives Pump_Active_1_Hour %M00621, as the %M00621 coil at the output of the GE UPCTR block did. It needs its own rung because a CTU done bit is a counter member, not a BOOL tag.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(CTR_Pump_A_Hour.DN)OTE(Pump_Active_1_Hour);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 9 (GE), page 2 row 807.48 - derived: R input of the UPCTR, NC %M00035, NO %M00700, NO %M00621]
Reset input R of the pump A active-hour counter: 7503-FS-001 stop foam button not inhibited (located NC, %M00035), System_Reset %M00700, or the counter's own done bit Pump_Active_1_Hour %M00621 reset the accumulated value. A Logix CTU has no reset pin, so this is RES(CTR_Pump_A_Hour) with the same conditioning logic.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIO(FS_7503_001_ALI),XIC(System_Reset),XIC(Pump_Active_1_Hour)]RES(CTR_Pump_A_Hour);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 11 (GE), page 3 row 305.64 - NO %M00229 -> ONDTR TENTHS %T00003 (Pump_Timer1 %R00209) PV 300; R input: NO %M00395, NC %M00229]
Pump A deluge retry timer: GE ONDTR TENTHS %T00003 (retentive on-delay, register Pump_Timer1 %R00209) with preset 300 tenths = 30000 ms = 30 s, converted to TON tag TMR_T00003. The R input of the block is wired to 7503-PST-001 deluge line pressure high %M00395 or PUMP_A_INT %M00229 dropping out (see the RES rung below); because the reset is asserted whenever the pump is off, the accumulated value is in practice never retained across a pump stop.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(PUMP_A_INT)TON(TMR_T00003,30000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 11 (GE), page 3 row 305.64 - derived: R input of the ONDTR, NO %M00395 parallel NC %M00229 -> RES TMR_T00003]
Reset input R of ONDTR %T00003: 7503-PST-001 deluge line pressure high %M00395 or PUMP_A_INT %M00229 off resets the timer in the GE program (boolean reset pin of the ONDTR block). Converted to RES(TMR_T00003) because a Logix TON has no reset pin; the MOVE WORD 0 into Pump_Timer1 %R00209 elsewhere in the program does the same job in the source.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(PST_7503_001_ALHI),XIO(PUMP_A_INT)]RES(TMR_T00003);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 12 (GE), page 3 row 695.88 - NO %T00003 -> TMR TENTHS %T00004 (Pump_Timer2 %R00212) PV 20]
Pump B retry pulse 1: GE TMR TENTHS %T00004 (non-retentive on-delay, register Pump_Timer2 %R00212) with preset 20 tenths = 2000 ms = 2 s, converted to TON tag TMR_T00004. It starts as soon as the 30-second retry timer %T00003 is done and provides the first 2-second start pulse to pump B.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_T00003.DN)TON(TMR_T00004,2000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 13 (GE), page 3 row 947.16 - NO %T00004 -> TMR TENTHS %T00005 (Pump_Timer3 %R00215) PV 600]
Pump B retry wait 2: GE TMR TENTHS %T00005 (non-retentive on-delay, register Pump_Timer3 %R00215) with preset 600 tenths = 60000 ms = 60 s - raised from 30 s to 60 s on 12-june-03 - converted to TON tag TMR_T00005. It runs on after the first 2-second start pulse %T00004.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_T00004.DN)TON(TMR_T00005,60000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 14 (GE), page 4 row 32.76 - NO %T00005 -> TMR TENTHS %T00006 (Pump_Timer4 %R00218) PV 20]
Pump B retry pulse 2: GE TMR TENTHS %T00006 (non-retentive on-delay, register Pump_Timer4 %R00218) with preset 20 tenths = 2000 ms = 2 s, converted to TON tag TMR_T00006; second 2-second start pulse to pump B after the 60-second wait %T00005.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_T00005.DN)TON(TMR_T00006,2000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 15 (GE), page 4 row 284.04 - NO %T00006 -> TMR TENTHS %T00007 (Pump_Timer5 %R00221) PV 600]
Pump B retry wait 3: GE TMR TENTHS %T00007 (non-retentive on-delay, register Pump_Timer5 %R00221) with preset 600 tenths = 60000 ms = 60 s, converted to TON tag TMR_T00007; third waiting period of the pump B start sequence.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_T00006.DN)TON(TMR_T00007,60000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 16 (GE), page 4 row 535.32 - NO %T00007 -> TMR TENTHS %T00008 (Pump_Timer6 %R00224) PV 20]
Pump B retry pulse 3: GE TMR TENTHS %T00008 (non-retentive on-delay, register Pump_Timer6 %R00224) with preset 20 tenths = 2000 ms = 2 s, converted to TON tag TMR_T00008; third and last 2-second start pulse to pump B.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_T00007.DN)TON(TMR_T00008,2000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="13" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 17 (GE), page 4 row 786.60 - branches NO %T00003/NC %T00004, NO %T00005/NC %T00006, NO %T00007/NC %T00008 -> OTE %M00231]
Pump B start pulses: PUMP_B_START_INT %M00231 is true during the 2 seconds between a retry timer timing out and its pulse timer timing out - %T00003 done with %T00004 not yet done, %T00005 done with %T00006 not yet done, or %T00007 done with %T00008 not yet done. The three series branches are drawn on separate rows joined by a vertical wire and are OR-ed.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(TMR_T00003.DN)XIO(TMR_T00004.DN),XIC(TMR_T00005.DN)XIO(TMR_T00006.DN),XIC(TMR_T00007.DN)XIO(TMR_T00008.DN)]OTE(PUMP_B_START_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="14" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 18 (GE), page 5 row 32.76 - NO %T00008 -> ONDTR TENTHS (Pump_Timer7 %R00227) PV 600 -> OTE %M00620; R input: NO %M00395, NC %T00008]
Deluge-failed-to-release delay: GE ONDTR TENTHS with register Pump_Timer7 %R00227 (retentive on-delay) and preset 600 tenths = 60000 ms = 60 s, converted to TON tag TMR_DelugeFail. It starts on the third pump B start pulse %T00008 and, if the deluge line has still not released within 60 s, sets the panel alarm DelugeFailedToRelease %M00620. As in rung 11 the R input also includes %T00008 dropping out, so the retained value cannot survive the end of the pulse.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_T00008.DN)TON(TMR_DelugeFail,60000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="15" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 18 (GE), page 5 row 32.76 - derived: ONDTR output coil -> OTE %M00620]
Output coil of the ONDTR block: its done state drives DelugeFailedToRelease %M00620, the 'Deluge failed to release' alarm bit. Separate rung because the TON is already the output instruction of the rung above.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_DelugeFail.DN)OTE(DelugeFailedToRelease);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="16" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 18 (GE), page 5 row 32.76 - derived: R input of the ONDTR, NO %M00395 parallel NC %T00008 -> RES TMR_DelugeFail]
Reset input R of the ONDTR Pump_Timer7 %R00227: 7503-PST-001 deluge line pressure high %M00395 (deluge released) or %T00008 dropping out resets it. Converted to RES(TMR_DelugeFail) because a Logix TON has no reset pin.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(PST_7503_001_ALHI),XIO(TMR_T00008.DN)]RES(TMR_DelugeFail);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="17" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 20 (GE), page 5 row 528.60 - NC %M00388 %M00389 %M00396 %M00398 in series -> TMR TENTHS %T00009 (Pump_Timer8 %R00230) PV 20]
Pump B stop delay: with none of the fire causes active - 7404-DF-001 %M00388, 7404-DF-002 %M00389, 7503-FR-001/002 %M00396 and 7503-FR-003 %M00398 all normal, located NC in series - the GE TMR TENTHS %T00009 (non-retentive on-delay, register Pump_Timer8 %R00230) with preset 20 tenths = 2000 ms = 2 s produces the 2-second stop pulse, converted to TON tag TMR_T00009.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(DF_7404_001_ALHI)XIO(DF_7404_002_ALHI)XIO(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI)XIO(FR_7503_003_ALHI)TON(TMR_T00009,2000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="18" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: CE_LOG rung 21 (GE), page 5 row 868.68 - NC %M00035 parallel (NC %M00388 %M00389 %M00396 %M00398 %T00009 in series) -> OTE %M00230]
Stop of pump B: the stop foam button 7503-FS-001 not inhibited (%M00035, NC) or all fire causes back to normal (7404-DF-001 %M00388, 7404-DF-002 %M00389, 7503-FR-001/002 %M00396, 7503-FR-003 %M00398 NC in series) together with the 2-second stop delay %T00009 sets PUMP_B_STOP_INT %M00230.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIO(FS_7503_001_ALI),XIO(DF_7404_001_ALHI)XIO(DF_7404_002_ALHI)XIO(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI)XIO(FR_7503_003_ALHI)XIO(TMR_T00009.DN)]OTE(PUMP_B_STOP_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="19" Type="N">
