              <Rung Number="31" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 36 (GE) - System_Sound01..System_Sound31 (31 NOCON, %M00800..%M00830) -> SETCOIL Tag_DO_15_INT %M00239; group banner is rung 35 'Sound on panel in Production Control Room (buzzer):']
Panel buzzer latch: 31 NO contacts in parallel - System_Sound01 (%M00800) on the main row plus the five-per-row groups 02/08/13/18/23, 03/09/14/19/24, 04/10/15/20/25, 05/11/16/21/26, 06/12/17/22/27 and 07/28/29/30/31 on the six rows below - so ANY sound pulse sets Tag_DO_15_INT (%M00239, 'Panel alarm - Internal C_E use'). It is an OTL latch and only rung 49 clears it; the sound-on-panel banner of rung 35 is what names this output.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(System_Sound01),XIC(System_Sound02),XIC(System_Sound08),XIC(System_Sound13),XIC(System_Sound18),XIC(System_Sound23),XIC(System_Sound03),XIC(System_Sound09),XIC(System_Sound14),XIC(System_Sound19),XIC(System_Sound24),XIC(System_Sound04),XIC(System_Sound10),XIC(System_Sound15),XIC(System_Sound20),XIC(System_Sound25),XIC(System_Sound05),XIC(System_Sound11),XIC(System_Sound16),XIC(System_Sound21),XIC(System_Sound26),XIC(System_Sound06),XIC(System_Sound12),XIC(System_Sound17),XIC(System_Sound22),XIC(System_Sound27),XIC(System_Sound07),XIC(System_Sound28),XIC(System_Sound29),XIC(System_Sound30),XIC(System_Sound31)]OTL(Tag_DO_15_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="32" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 38 (GE) - System_Sound01..System_Sound26 (26 NOCON, %M00800..%M00825) -> SETCOIL SA_7404_001_002_INT %M00226; group banner is rung 37 'Alarm Bell in Pump House:']
Pump-house alarm bell latch: the same auto-wrapped parallel group as rung 36 but restricted to the first 26 sound bits (System_Sound01 %M00800 on the main row, then 02/08/13/18/23, 03/09/14/19/24, 04/10/15/20/25, 05/11/16/21/26, 06/12/17/22 and 07 on the rows below), so ANY of them sets SA_7404_001_002_INT (%M00226, '7404-SA-001/002 Local alarm pump house - Internal C_E use'). System_Sound27..31 and 32..37/40 are intentionally excluded, matching the rung-2 history note.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(System_Sound01),XIC(System_Sound02),XIC(System_Sound08),XIC(System_Sound13),XIC(System_Sound18),XIC(System_Sound23),XIC(System_Sound03),XIC(System_Sound09),XIC(System_Sound14),XIC(System_Sound19),XIC(System_Sound24),XIC(System_Sound04),XIC(System_Sound10),XIC(System_Sound15),XIC(System_Sound20),XIC(System_Sound25),XIC(System_Sound05),XIC(System_Sound11),XIC(System_Sound16),XIC(System_Sound21),XIC(System_Sound26),XIC(System_Sound06),XIC(System_Sound12),XIC(System_Sound17),XIC(System_Sound22),XIC(System_Sound07)]OTL(SA_7404_001_002_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="33" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 40 (GE) - #BAD_RAM (%SB0010) NOCON, POSCOIL System_Sound32 (%M00831)]
NO contact #BAD_RAM (%SB0010) drives the positive-transition (one-shot) coil System_Sound32 (%M00831): CPU system bit #BAD_RAM (bad RAM). Its rising edge pulses System_Sound32 for one scan and that pulse is one of the seven parallel inputs that latch PLC_Fault_INT in rung 47; it is outside both sound-latch groups (rung 36 takes System_Sound01..31, rung 38 takes 01..26).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SYS_BAD_RAM)ONS(System_Sound32_OS)OTE(System_Sound32);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="34" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 41 (GE) - #HRD_CPU (%SA0010) NOCON, POSCOIL System_Sound33 (%M00832)]
NO contact #HRD_CPU (%SA0010) drives the positive-transition (one-shot) coil System_Sound33 (%M00832): CPU system bit #HRD_CPU (hardware fault - CPU). Its rising edge pulses System_Sound33 for one scan and that pulse is one of the seven parallel inputs that latch PLC_Fault_INT in rung 47; it is outside both sound-latch groups (rung 36 takes System_Sound01..31, rung 38 takes 01..26).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SYS_HRD_CPU)ONS(System_Sound33_OS)OTE(System_Sound33);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="35" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 42 (GE) - #HRD_FLT (%SC0014) NOCON, POSCOIL System_Sound34 (%M00833)]
NO contact #HRD_FLT (%SC0014) drives the positive-transition (one-shot) coil System_Sound34 (%M00833): CPU system bit #HRD_FLT (hardware fault - fault table). Its rising edge pulses System_Sound34 for one scan and that pulse is one of the seven parallel inputs that latch PLC_Fault_INT in rung 47; it is outside both sound-latch groups (rung 36 takes System_Sound01..31, rung 38 takes 01..26).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SYS_HRD_FLT)ONS(System_Sound34_OS)OTE(System_Sound34);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="36" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 43 (GE) - #LOS_IOM (%SA0014) NOCON, POSCOIL System_Sound35 (%M00834)]
NO contact #LOS_IOM (%SA0014) drives the positive-transition (one-shot) coil System_Sound35 (%M00834): CPU system bit #LOS_IOM (loss of an I/O module). Its rising edge pulses System_Sound35 for one scan and that pulse is one of the seven parallel inputs that latch PLC_Fault_INT in rung 47; it is outside both sound-latch groups (rung 36 takes System_Sound01..31, rung 38 takes 01..26).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SYS_LOS_IOM)ONS(System_Sound35_OS)OTE(System_Sound35);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="37" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 44 (GE) - #LOS_RCK (%SA0012) NOCON, POSCOIL System_Sound36 (%M00835)]
NO contact #LOS_RCK (%SA0012) drives the positive-transition (one-shot) coil System_Sound36 (%M00835): CPU system bit #LOS_RCK (loss of rack). Its rising edge pulses System_Sound36 for one scan and that pulse is one of the seven parallel inputs that latch PLC_Fault_INT in rung 47; it is outside both sound-latch groups (rung 36 takes System_Sound01..31, rung 38 takes 01..26).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SYS_LOS_RCK)ONS(System_Sound36_OS)OTE(System_Sound36);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="38" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 45 (GE) - #LOW_BAT (%SA0011) NOCON, POSCOIL System_Sound37 (%M00836)]
NO contact #LOW_BAT (%SA0011) drives the positive-transition (one-shot) coil System_Sound37 (%M00836): CPU system bit #LOW_BAT (low battery). Its rising edge pulses System_Sound37 for one scan and that pulse is one of the seven parallel inputs that latch PLC_Fault_INT in rung 47; it is outside both sound-latch groups (rung 36 takes System_Sound01..31, rung 38 takes 01..26).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SYS_LOW_BAT)ONS(System_Sound37_OS)OTE(System_Sound37);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="39" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 46 (GE) - Pump_B_Inhibited_AL (%M00009) NOCON, POSCOIL System_Sound40 (%M00839)]
NO contact Pump_B_Inhibited_AL (%M00009) drives the positive-transition (one-shot) coil System_Sound40 (%M00839): standby pump B inhibited - alarm. Its rising edge pulses System_Sound40 for one scan and that pulse is one of the seven parallel inputs that latch PLC_Fault_INT in rung 47; it is outside both sound-latch groups (rung 36 takes System_Sound01..31, rung 38 takes 01..26).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_B_Inhibited_AL)ONS(System_Sound40_OS)OTE(System_Sound40);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="40" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 47 (GE) - System_Sound32, 33, 35, 37, 34, 36, 40 (7 NOCON, %M00831..%M00839) -> SETCOIL PLC_Fault_INT %M00240]
PLC fault sound latch: 7 NO contacts in parallel - System_Sound32 (%M00831, bad RAM) on the main row, System_Sound33/35/37 (%M00832/%M00834/%M00836) on the first branch row and System_Sound34/36/40 (%M00833/%M00835/%M00839) on the second - so any PLC system-fault sound pulse sets PLC_Fault_INT (%M00240, 'Set when PLC fault exists - Internal C_E use'). Latched by OTL here and cleared only by the three reset coils of rung 49.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(System_Sound32),XIC(System_Sound33),XIC(System_Sound35),XIC(System_Sound37),XIC(System_Sound34),XIC(System_Sound36),XIC(System_Sound40)]OTL(PLC_Fault_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="41" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 49 (GE) part 1/3 - System_Reset %M00700 NOCON (main row) in parallel with System_Mute %M00706 NOCON (branch row) -> RESETCOIL Tag_DO_15_INT %M00239]
Reset of all sounds (banner rung 48): NO System_Reset (%M00700) on the main row and NO System_Mute (%M00706, 'System Mute from tuch panel') on the branch row are in parallel and their common node feeds this RESET coil on the main row, clearing Tag_DO_15_INT (%M00239). Part 1 of 3 - the printed rung drives three RESET coils from the one condition and a Logix v17 rung may hold a single output, so the condition is repeated unchanged on each part.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(System_Reset),XIC(System_Mute)]OTU(Tag_DO_15_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="42" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 49 (GE) part 2/3 - System_Reset %M00700 NOCON (main row) in parallel with System_Mute %M00706 NOCON (branch row) -> RESETCOIL SA_7404_001_002_INT %M00226]
Reset of all sounds (banner rung 48): NO System_Reset (%M00700) on the main row and NO System_Mute (%M00706, 'System Mute from tuch panel') on the branch row are in parallel and their common node feeds this RESET coil on the branch row, fed over the x=602 bus, clearing SA_7404_001_002_INT (%M00226). Part 2 of 3 - the printed rung drives three RESET coils from the one condition and a Logix v17 rung may hold a single output, so the condition is repeated unchanged on each part.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(System_Reset),XIC(System_Mute)]OTU(SA_7404_001_002_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="43" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Sound rung 49 (GE) part 3/3 - System_Reset %M00700 NOCON (main row) in parallel with System_Mute %M00706 NOCON (branch row) -> RESETCOIL PLC_Fault_INT %M00240]
Reset of all sounds (banner rung 48): NO System_Reset (%M00700) on the main row and NO System_Mute (%M00706, 'System Mute from tuch panel') on the branch row are in parallel and their common node feeds this RESET coil on the row below the branch row, fed over the x=602 bus, clearing PLC_Fault_INT (%M00240). Part 3 of 3 - the printed rung drives three RESET coils from the one condition and a Logix v17 rung may hold a single output, so the condition is repeated unchanged on each part.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(System_Reset),XIC(System_Mute)]OTU(PLC_Fault_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="44" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Alarm Mute/Silence: Activated by physical pushbutton E12 on panel door (TB-07 23&24)]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Mute_Alm_PB)OTE(System_Mute);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Output" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Output rung 3 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL Shutdow]
Unconditional call of the Shutdow block, which sets the physical shutdown outputs (printed legend: 'Call Output block for Shutdown.'). #ALW_ON (%S00007) is always true, so the JSR is unconditional; the routine name is spelled `Shutdow` exactly as printed in the CALL operand.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(Shutdow,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Output rung 5 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL Protect]
Unconditional call of the Protect block, which drives the fire-protection outputs (printed legend: 'Call Output block for Fire Protection.').]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(Protect,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Output rung 7 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL Indicat]
Unconditional call of the Indicat block, which drives the panel indication outputs (printed legend: 'Call Output block for indication.').]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(Indicat,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Output rung 9 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL Loc_Al]
Unconditional call of the Loc_Al block, which drives the local (pump house) alarm outputs (printed legend: 'Call Output block for  Local alarms.'). The target keeps the printed spelling `Loc_Al`.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(Loc_Al,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Output rung 11 (GE) - %S00007 (#ALW_ON) NOCON; CALL FLT_1]
Unconditional call of the FLT_1 block, which handles line fault on the outputs (printed legend: 'Call Output block FLT_1 for  Line fault on Outputs.').]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(FLT_1,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Map program output tags to physical digital output module (Slot 8 DO)]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[JSR(IO_Mapping_Out,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Shutdow" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Shutdow rung 3 (GE) part 1/1 - %M00225, %M00161, %M00045 -> %Q00001; NCCON, NOCON, NOCON -> COIL (plain OTE, NOT inverted)]
6401-EY-001/002 ESD fuel gas valve shutdown: the internal cause-and-effect bit EY_6401_001_002_INT (%M00225) is printed NC, so the output EY_6401_001_002 (%Q00001) drops when the trip is demanded and can only stay energised while the manual-trip bit EY_6401_001_002_MT (%M00161) is set. The parallel branch forces the output back to 1 when the all-outputs inhibit INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI (%M00045) is set. The printed coil is a plain OTE - this rung is not inverted.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIO(EY_6401_001_002_INT)XIC(EY_6401_001_002_MT),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)]OTE(EY_6401_001_002);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[Fire & Gas pump shutdown output (Fail-Safe Active-Low): normally energized (1). De-energizes to 0 (trips) when PumpShutdown_INT is active, unless bypassed by INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI (matches GE NCCOIL).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIO(PumpShutdown_INT),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)]OTE(PumpShutdown);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[P2100/P2200 oil booster pump shutdown output (Fail-Safe Active-Low): normally energized (1). De-energizes to 0 (trips) when P2100_P2200_INT is active, unless bypassed by INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI (matches GE NCCOIL).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIO(P2100_P2200_INT),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)]OTE(P2100_P2200);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[P3600/P3700 water booster pump shutdown output (Fail-Safe Active-Low): normally energized (1). De-energizes to 0 (trips) when P3600_P3700_INT is active, unless bypassed by INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI (matches GE NCCOIL).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIO(P3600_P3700_INT),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)]OTE(P3600_P3700);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Protect" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 2 (GE) part 1/1 - %M00229, %M00044, %M00045 -> %Q00005; NOCON, NCCON, NCCON -> COIL]
Deluge pump A start/stop internal cause-and-effect bit PUMP_A_INT (%M00229) drives the field output PUMP_A (%Q00005) through the foam-release inhibit INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI (%M00044) and the all-outputs inhibit INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI (%M00045); both inhibits are printed NC so they are XIO. Page banner for this part of the block: 'Fire Protection Outputs set in this block.']]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(PUMP_A_INT)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI)XIO(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)OTE(PUMP_A);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 3 (GE) part 1/1 - %M00231, %M00044, %M00045 -> %Q00007; NOCON, NCCON, NCCON -> COIL]
Deluge pump B start internal cause-and-effect bit PUMP_B_START_INT (%M00231) drives the field output PUMP_B_START (%Q00007) through the same two NC inhibits, INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI (%M00044) and INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI (%M00045).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(PUMP_B_START_INT)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI)XIO(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)OTE(PUMP_B_START);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 4 (GE) part 1/1 - %M00230 -> %Q00006; NOCON -> COIL]
Deluge pump B stop internal cause-and-effect bit PUMP_B_STOP_INT (%M00230) drives the field output PUMP_B_STOP (%Q00006) directly - this is the only one of the three pump output rungs with no inhibit contact printed on it.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(PUMP_B_STOP_INT)OTE(PUMP_B_STOP);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 7 (GE) part 1/3 - R pin: NC %S00006 -> RES of the timer for Pump_Timer11 %R00239]
Reset pin of the rung 7 ONDTR block: the NC #T_MIN (%S00006) contact printed on the row below the block resets the 28 s check timer. Implemented as RES on the timer helper, placed before the timer so a done bit cannot be copied to %T00013 in the same scan as the reset.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(T_MIN_PULSE)RES(TMR_Pump_Timer11);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 7 (GE) part 2/3 - %T00002, %S00006 -> ONDTR_TENTHS Pump_Timer11 %R00239 PV 280]
Open-circuit check timer for the pump A start signal: ONDTR TENTHS block Pump_Timer11 (%R00239), PV 280 = 28.0 s, enabled by T00002 (%T00002, high 120 s after run) in series with the #T_MIN 1-minute pulse contact. Converted to TON with the preset in milliseconds (28000), so the 28 s delay is unchanged.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(T00002)XIC(T_MIN_PULSE)TON(TMR_Pump_Timer11,28000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 7 (GE) part 3/3 - timer output -> %T00013 COIL]
The block's output pin drives the %T00013 coil ('For checking Open circuit on Start Pump'); reproduced by copying the timer's done bit to %T00013, which stays a BOOL tag so the contact printed in rung 8 reads exactly as in the source.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_Pump_Timer11.DN)OTE(T00013);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 8 (GE) part 1/1 - %T00013, %T00002, %Q00005 -> %M00233; NOCON x3 -> COIL]
First pulse output for the %Q00005 open-circuit test: Pump_A_PulsOut_INT (%M00233) is set when the 28 s check timer %T00013 is done and the 120 s power-up block %T00002 is done, or immediately when the pump A output %Q00005 is already on (the PUMP_A branch hangs from the left rail and joins after %T00002).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(T00013)XIC(T00002),XIC(PUMP_A)]OTE(Pump_A_PulsOut_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 9 (GE) part 1/3 - R pin: NO %M00038 parallel NO %M00229 -> RES of the timer for Pump_Timer9 %R00233]
Reset pin of the rung 9 ONDTR block: the pulse readback Pump_A_PulsIn_ALI (%M00038) and the pump A output PUMP_A_INT (%M00229) are printed NO and are fed from the left rail, so either one resets the 70 s open-circuit timer as soon as a test pulse is read back.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn_ALI),XIC(PUMP_A_INT)]RES(TMR_Pump_Timer9);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 9 (GE) part 2/3 - %T00002 -> ONDTR_TENTHS Pump_Timer9 %R00233 PV 700]
Open-circuit detection for the %Q0005 start/stop signal: ONDTR TENTHS block Pump_Timer9 (%R00233), PV 700 = 70.0 s, times while %T00002 is done; converted to TON with preset 70000 ms (the printed note reads 'If puls on input not registered in 70 seconds (1min + 10 sec) -> set Open circuit bit for %Q0005').]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(T00002)TON(TMR_Pump_Timer9,70000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 9 (GE) part 3/3 - timer output -> %M00293 COIL]
The block's output pin drives PUMP_A_OC (%M00293), 'Deluge pump A Start/Stop - Open circuit' - the pump A open-circuit alarm, reproduced by copying the timer's done bit to the %M bit.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_Pump_Timer9.DN)OTE(PUMP_A_OC);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 11 (GE) part 1/3 - R pin: NC %S00006 -> RES of the timer for Pump_Timer12 %R00242]
Reset pin of the rung 11 ONDTR block: the NC #T_MIN (%S00006) contact printed on the row below the block resets the 28 s check timer for the pump B start signal; implemented as RES placed before the timer for the same reason as rung 7.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIO(T_MIN_PULSE)RES(TMR_Pump_Timer12);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 11 (GE) part 2/3 - %T00002, %S00006 -> ONDTR_TENTHS Pump_Timer12 %R00242 PV 280]
Open-circuit check timer for the pump B start signal: ONDTR TENTHS block Pump_Timer12 (%R00242), PV 280 = 28.0 s, enabled by %T00002 in series with the #T_MIN pulse contact; converted to TON with preset 28000 ms.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(T00002)XIC(T_MIN_PULSE)TON(TMR_Pump_Timer12,28000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 11 (GE) part 3/3 - timer output -> %T00014 COIL]
The block's output pin drives the %T00014 coil ('For checking Open circuit on Start Pump'); reproduced by copying the timer's done bit to %T00014, which stays a BOOL tag read by the contact in rung 12.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_Pump_Timer12.DN)OTE(T00014);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="13" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 12 (GE) part 1/1 - %T00014, %T00002, %Q00007 -> %M00234; NOCON x3 -> COIL]
First pulse output for the %Q00007 open-circuit test: Pump_B_Start_PulsOut_INT (%M00234) is set when the 28 s check timer %T00014 is done and %T00002 is done, or immediately when the pump B start output %Q00007 is already on (parallel branch from the left rail joining after %T00002).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[[XIC(T00014)XIC(T00002),XIC(PUMP_B_START)]OTE(Pump_B_Start_PulsOut_INT);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="14" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 13 (GE) part 1/3 - R pin: NO %M00039 -> RES of the timer for Pump_Timer10 %R00236]
Reset pin of the rung 13 ONDTR block: the pulse readback Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_ALI (%M00039) is printed NO from the left rail and resets the 70 s open-circuit timer whenever a test pulse is read back.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_ALI)RES(TMR_Pump_Timer10);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="15" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 13 (GE) part 2/3 - %T00002 -> ONDTR_TENTHS Pump_Timer10 %R00236 PV 700]
Open-circuit detection for the %Q0007 start signal: ONDTR TENTHS block Pump_Timer10 (%R00236), PV 700 = 70.0 s, times while %T00002 is done; converted to TON with preset 70000 ms (printed note: 'If puls on input not registered in 70 seconds (1min + 10 sec) -> set Open circuit bit for %Q0007').]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(T00002)TON(TMR_Pump_Timer10,70000,0);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="16" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Protect rung 13 (GE) part 3/3 - timer output -> %M00295 COIL]
The block's output pin drives PUMP_B_START_OC (%M00295), 'Deluge pump B Start - Open circuit' - the pump B start open-circuit alarm, reproduced by copying the timer's done bit to the %M bit.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(TMR_Pump_Timer10.DN)OTE(PUMP_B_START_OC);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Indicat" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Indicat rung 2 (GE) - NOCON Tag_DO_13_INT %M00237 -> COIL Tag_DO_13 %Q00013]
Single NO contact Tag_DO_13_INT (%M00237, 'EDS valve closed indication - Internal C_E use') drives the unlatched output coil Tag_DO_13 (%Q00013, 'EDS valve closed indication'). The local panel indication simply mirrors the internal cause & effect bit.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Tag_DO_13_INT)OTE(Tag_DO_13);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Indicat rung 3 (GE) - NOCON Tag_DO_12_INT %M00236 -> COIL Tag_DO_12 %Q00012]
Single NO contact Tag_DO_12_INT (%M00236, 'EDS valve open indication - Internal C_E use') drives the unlatched output coil Tag_DO_12 (%Q00012, 'EDS valve open indication').]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Tag_DO_12_INT)OTE(Tag_DO_12);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Indicat rung 4 (GE) - NOCON Tag_DO_14_INT %M00238 -> COIL Tag_DO_14 %Q00014]
Single NO contact Tag_DO_14_INT (%M00238, 'EDS valve low air indication - Internal C_E use') drives the unlatched output coil Tag_DO_14 (%Q00014, 'EDS valve low air indication').]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Tag_DO_14_INT)OTE(Tag_DO_14);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Loc_Al" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Loc_Al rung 2 (GE) - NOCON SA_7404_001_002_INT %M00226 series NCCON INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI %M00044 -> COIL SA_7404_001_002 %Q00002]
Series chain: NO contact SA_7404_001_002_INT (%M00226, '7404-SA-001/002 Local alarm pump house - Internal C_E use') followed by NC contact INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI (%M00044, 'Foam release inhibit - Alarm inhibit'), driving the unlatched output coil SA_7404_001_002 (%Q00002, '7404-SA-001/002 Local alarm pump house'). The local alarm output follows the internal bit unless the foam release / alarm inhibit is active, in which case it is forced off.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(SA_7404_001_002_INT)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI)OTE(SA_7404_001_002);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Loc_Al rung 3 (GE) - NOCON Tag_DO_15_INT %M00239 series NCCON INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI %M00044 -> COIL Tag_DO_15 %Q00015]
Series chain: NO contact Tag_DO_15_INT (%M00239, 'Panel alarm - Internal C_E use') followed by the same NC contact INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI (%M00044), driving the output coil Tag_DO_15 (%Q00015, 'Panel alarm'). The panel alarm output is therefore also suppressed while the foam release / alarm inhibit is active.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Tag_DO_15_INT)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI)OTE(Tag_DO_15);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: Loc_Al rung 4 (GE) - NOCON PLC_Fault_INT %M00240 series NCCON Tag_DO_15 %Q00015 -> COIL PLC_Fault %Q00016]
Series chain: NO contact PLC_Fault_INT (%M00240, 'Set when PLC fault exists - Internal C_E use') followed by the NC contact Tag_DO_15 (%Q00015), driving the output coil PLC_Fault (%Q00016, 'SpareDO-16'). Note the second contact has no inhibit in this rung: it is a NC contact on the Tag_DO_15 output bit itself, so the PLC fault output is blocked while the local panel alarm is energised.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(PLC_Fault_INT)XIO(Tag_DO_15)OTE(PLC_Fault);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="FLT_1" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: FLT_1 rung 3 (GE) - NOCON Pump_A_PulsOut_INT %M00233 -> COIL Pump_A_PulsOut %Q00009]
Single NO contact Pump_A_PulsOut_INT (%M00233, 'Pulsed output for open circuit check on Pump A Out signal - Internal use') drives the unlatched output coil Pump_A_PulsOut (%Q00009, 'Pulsed output for open circuit check on Pump A Out signal'). The pulsed output is what allows an open-circuit line fault to be detected on the pump A start/stop output.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_A_PulsOut_INT)OTE(Pump_A_PulsOut);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
                  <![CDATA[[Source: FLT_1 rung 5 (GE) - NOCON Pump_B_Start_PulsOut_INT %M00234 -> COIL Pump_B_Start_PulsOut %Q00010]
Single NO contact Pump_B_Start_PulsOut_INT (%M00234, 'Pulsed output for open circuit check on Pump B Start signal - Internal use') drives the unlatched output coil Pump_B_Start_PulsOut (%Q00010, 'Pulsed output for open circuit check on Pump B Start signal'). Same line-fault pulse arrangement as rung 3, for pump B.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
                  <![CDATA[XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsOut_INT)OTE(Pump_B_Start_PulsOut);]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
